  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For an owner positioning a hotel around **differentiated guest experience** and **local character**, the strongest lifestyle brands to consider are **Hotel Indigo**, **Canopy by Hilton**, **The Hoxton**, **The Standard**, **The Dean**, **Palisociety**, **Andaz**, **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt**, **Moxy**, **Kimpton**, **SLH**, and **Edition**.[2][6][8][14][16][18][20]\n\nThe clearest brand fits for *local, neighborhood-led positioning* are:\n\n- **Hotel Indigo** — explicitly built around local culture and each property being different from the next, with neighborhood-specific design and storytelling.[2][16]\n- **Canopy by Hilton** — emphasizes connection to the local environment and often uses local art, materials, and destination-specific design cues.[2][17]\n- **The Hoxton** — positions hotels as open-house social hubs for guests and locals, with community-rooted programming and strong neighborhood energy.[6][8]\n- **The Dean** — described as characterful, design-led, and rooted in local culture and creative energy.[4]\n- **Palisociety** — known for neighborhood hotels that reflect the character and history of each location.[8]\n- **Andaz** — Hyatt’s lifestyle brand focused on personal style, locally sourced design elements, and guest-driven experiences.[14][20]\n- **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** — a collection of independent-style hotels with a destination-first approach and strong cultural immersion.[3]\n- **SLH (Small Luxury Hotels of the World)** — each hotel is positioned as a reflection of its surroundings and local heritage.[18]\n\nFor owners looking for a more *design-forward but still locally expressive* lifestyle angle, these are also relevant:\n\n- **Edition** — architecturally distinct properties that reflect local character within a luxury-lifestyle framework.[14][20]\n- **Kimpton** — often cited among global brands adapting boutique and locally inspired hotel concepts.[16]\n- **Moxy** — included among global brands that have found ways to scale individuality and boutique style.[16]\n- **The Standard** — known for bold design, destination dining, and cultural programming that draws locals as well as guests.[6]\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **brand-by-brand shortlist by scale, market segment, and owner fit**.",
